Most people would not...

We were discussing the choices of an early-game character not having 
found an altar to sacrifice or pray on.  Implicit in the discussion was, 
I suppose, that he was no longer at level 1, since otherwise there would 
be no need to become desperate, not having explored the dungeon down to 
Dlvl 10 or so.  So the protection racket was not an option any more.

> If you want cheap protection do the protection racket.

Which will kill you in at least half the cases, so in general is not a 
wise strategy.  And if you don't do it, protection is not as cheap and 
you want to keep the only priest alive.  But you'd have to kill him in 
order to be able to sacrifice or pray on his altar...  (providing he is 
not co-aligned).

> If you still want to sacrifice for an artifact, kill the mine town 
> priest after you've bought the protection.

That is not a choice, if buying the protection takes as long as it 
usually does.  You just have to forgo those protection points until you 
see the valley of the dead, if you want to get equipment for survival 
(holy water and, maybe, an artifact) from the altar.
